[2026-09-07 21:58:16] REQ 260907215043-63 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=126 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_6h5lkf4n","function":{"index":0,"name":"git_commit","arguments":{"repo_path":"/root/i.ar","message":"cross-response repetition guard (c111): catch deepseek text-only loop across responses\n\nThe per-response output-runaway guard (20 identical lines in ONE\nresponse) misses the deepseek-v4-flash text-only loop, which repeats\nthe SAME paragraph ACROSS responses (5-10 reps each, under the\nper-response threshold). The burn accumulates across ~22 requests /\n471k input tokens before the final 65536-token response trips the\ntruncated-output check.\n\nNew guard iar--cycle-cross-response-repetition-p tracks the\nmost-repeated trimmed line across the last N responses (window 5,\nthreshold 30 cumulative) via a sliding window of per-response\nline-count hashes stored in the state's :cross-rep-window. Fires the\nsame recovery path as the per-response runaway (sharing\n:runaway-recovery-given): one recovery round-trip, then end on second\nfire. Catches the loop at response ~5-6, saving ~17 requests of burn\nper occurrence.\n\nFixed a triangular-counting bug during development: adding the running\nper-response count (1,3,6,10...) instead of 1 per occurrence made 10\nidentical lines hit 55, not 10.\n\n5 new tests, suite 1076/1076 green."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[21:58:16] Success: Committed in /root/i.ar\n[main 35531f9] cross-response repetition guard (c111): catch deepseek text-only loop across responses\n 2 files changed, 247 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n create mode 100644 emacs.d/test/test-cross-response-repetition.el"}]
